      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1015",
      "html": "<p><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Leptodoras cataniai Sabaj Pérez, 2005</p><p><strong>Common name:</strong> Slank Musemalle (Denmark)</p><p><strong>Etymology:</strong> Leptodoras: from the Greek leptos, meaning slender, and doras, meaning skin (also a word commonly used in forming generic names for doradids); in reference to the shape. Named in honor of David Catania, for his dedicated service to the ichthyological community since 1985 as Collection Manager of Fishes, California Academy of Sciences.</p><p><strong>Size:</strong> 194 mm (7.6 in) SL.</p><p><strong>IUCN Red List category:</strong> Least Concern. Last assessed 2020.</p>"
    },
    {
